vLLM's gfx950 MXFP8 linear kernel compacts weight_scale to [N/32, K/32] when every 32 rows share their
scales (DeepSeek-V4 checkpoints). verl starts vLLM with dummy weights, whose scales always pass that test,
so the live parameter is compacted and every later MXFP8 refit fails with "FP8 refit re-derived
weight_scale as (N, K/32) ... but the live parameter is (N/32, K/32)". Make the compaction switchable
(VLLM_ROCM_MXFP8_BLOCK32_SCALES, default on as upstream); set VLLM_ROCM_MXFP8_BLOCK32_SCALES=0 for verl:
verl's MXFP8 weights carry one scale per row and 32 elements, which never compacts, so only the dummy
weights take the block-scaled path. v0.34.0 still decides from the scale values (unchanged from v0.32.0).
Applies to /workspace/vllm (vLLM v0.34.0): cd /workspace/vllm && git apply <this file>

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/rocm_native.py b/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/rocm_native.py
index f6d869e..3005dcb 100644
--- a/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/rocm_native.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/kernels/linear/mxfp8/rocm_native.py
@@ -471,7 +471,10 @@ class RocmDotScaledMxfp8LinearKernel(Mxfp8LinearKernel):
         weight_scale = layer.weight_scale.data[:N, :scale_k].contiguous()
         # rocm_mxfp8_block32_gemm's split-K varies with M.
         block_scale = (
-            None if envs.VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT else _as_block32_scale(weight_scale)
+            None
+            if envs.VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT
+            or __import__("os").environ.get("VLLM_ROCM_MXFP8_BLOCK32_SCALES", "1") == "0"
+            else _as_block32_scale(weight_scale)
         )
         if block_scale is not None:
             # Checkpoints with 32x32 scale blocks (DeepSeek V4/V4.1) get them
